message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Metastasis as Stochastic Spreading on Organ-to-Organ Anatomical Graphs: Adequacy of Local Tumour-Burden ODEs under Lumped Outputs"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  Does a local tumour-burden ordinary differential equation remain an adequate
  in-silico object once dissemination is posed as a stochastic process on an
  organ-to-organ anatomical graph, or do graph observables remain unidentified
  under current lumped outputs? This computational research thesis — not a
  clinical study, not a medical device — answers with Nile B.Sc. chapter
  structure and a toy five-node laboratory: conservative transfers vanish from
  a homogeneous linear lump; logistic-soil twins match the lump while first
  sites flip; Fisher ranks on six edges are sloppy from summed burden and
  full-rank only from site-wise state. Distinct from theses 01–04.
